{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"wc -l /Users/manoelgaldino/.codex/skills/adjudicate-review/SKILL.md /Users/manoelgaldino/.codex/skills/adjudicate-review/references/finding-schema.md && sed -n '1,240p' /Users/manoelgaldino/.codex/skills/adjudicate-review/references/finding-schema.md && printf '\\\\n--- project workflow remainder ---\\\\n' && sed -n '100,260p' CLAUDE.md && printf '\\\\n--- required JSON keys/values ---\\\\n' && sed -n '1,260p' reports/refine_ink_review_paper_v4_2026-09-14/execution/cross_country.json && printf '\\\\n--- sdid prereq ---\\\\n' && sed -n '1,300p' reports/refine_ink_review_paper_v4_2026-09-14/execution/sdid.json\"","aggregated_output":"     103 /Users/manoelgaldino/.codex/skills/adjudicate-review/SKILL.md\n      85 /Users/manoelgaldino/.codex/skills/adjudicate-review/references/finding-schema.md\n     188 total\n# Adjudication finding schema\n\nUse schema version `1.0`. The JSON record is authoritative; render the same information in Markdown for readers.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"schema_version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"adjudication_id\": \"paper-slug:sha12:round1\",\n  \"source\": {\n    \"reviewed_artifact\": \"paper.pdf\",\n    \"sha256\": \"64-lowercase-hex\",\n    \"artifact_intact\": true\n  },\n  \"contract\": {\n    \"required\": true,\n    \"path\": \"quality_reports/argument_contracts/paper/sha/argument_contract.json\",\n    \"sha256\": \"64-lowercase-hex\",\n    \"contract_id\": \"paper:sha12:round1\",\n    \"artifact_sha256\": \"64-lowercase-hex\",\n    \"status\": \"PASS\",\n    \"stale\": false\n  },\n  \"review_sources\": [\n    {\"review_id\": \"R1\", \"path\": \"review.md\", \"sha256\": \"64-lowercase-hex\"}\n  ],\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"finding_id\": \"R1-F001\",\n      \"source_review\": \"R1\",\n      \"quoted_finding\": \"Verbatim or faithful normalized finding\",\n      \"type\": \"overclaim\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"scientific_dimension\": \"scope\",\n      \"held_decision\": false,\n      \"status\": \"PARTIAL\",\n      \"source_locations\": [\"p. 12, paragraph 2\"],\n      \"defect_evidence\": [\"The sentence is broader than the estimate\"],\n      \"refuting_evidence\": [\"The abstract already limits the population\"],\n      \"mechanical_checks\": [],\n      \"reasoning\": \"The local sentence is broad, but the paper does not make the universal claim alleged by the reviewer.\",\n      \"proposed_fix_assessment\": \"safe\",\n      \"disposition\": \"Narrow only the local sentence.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"summary\": {\n    \"total\": 1,\n    \"confirmed\": 0,\n    \"partial\": 1,\n    \"refuted\": 0,\n    \"unresolved\": 0,\n    \"held_decisions\": 0\n  },\n  \"adjudication\": {\n    \"verdict\": \"READY_FOR_IMPLEMENTATION\",\n    \"checked_at\": \"2026-08-27T12:00:00-03:00\",\n    \"reasons\": [\"One bounded partial defect is ready for implementation\"]\n  }\n}\n```\n\nWhen no argument contract is required, keep the `contract` object and set:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"required\": false,\n  \"path\": null,\n  \"sha256\": null,\n  \"contract_id\": null,\n  \"artifact_sha256\": null,\n  \"status\": null,\n  \"stale\": false\n}\n```\n\nAllowed `proposed_fix_assessment` values are `safe`, `unsafe`, `owner_decision`, `not_provided`, and `needs_design`.\n\n## Markdown rendering\n\n1. Source and contract identity\n2. Executive disposition\n3. Findings table\n4. Evidence and reasoning by finding\n5. Unsafe fixes and owner decisions\n6. Unresolved items\n7. Adjudication verdict\n\n--- project workflow remainder ---\n  raw data/                    # Dados brutos (24 subdirs)\n  output/                      # PDFs compilados, logs, figuras\n  references/                  # PDFs de papers citados\n  replication package/         # Pacote de replicacao para submissao\n  presentations/               # Slides\n  quality_reports/             # Reviews\n```\n\n## Stack\n- R (renv para dependencias, targets pipeline, fixest)\n- Execucao via `targets::tar_make()`\n- Cache local: `folha_scrape_cache.rds`, `wb_data_cache.rds` (determinismo sem API)\n- Dados: Dataverse DOI https://doi.org/10.7910/DVN/M97OCJ\n\n## Regras de trabalho\n\n### Separacao de papeis\n- **O agente que implementa NAO revisa. Quem revisa NAO implementa.** Usar agentes separados para cada funcao.\n\n### Autoria\n- **O autor escreve o paper.** NAO redigir secoes ou texto a menos que o autor peca explicitamente.\n- Em prosa de manuscrito e relatórios para o autor/leitor, evitar o jargão `spell`/`treatment spell`. Usar `treatment entry/onset`, `treated periods`, ou descrição substantiva do parceiro deslocado. `Spell` pode aparecer apenas como nome interno herdado de variável/arquivo quando tecnicamente necessário.\n\n### Workflow\n- NAO rodar scripts sem aprovacao do usuario\n- NAO commitar sem instrucao explicita\n- NAO incorrer custos de API externos sem aprovacao explicita previa (informar: o que, quantas chamadas, custo estimado)\n- Skills que exigem permissao devem ser rodadas em foreground\n- Sempre ler o arquivo antes de propor mudancas\n- Para imagens e documentos digitalizados, usar Read tool (VLM) diretamente — zero custo adicional\n\n--- required JSON keys/values ---\n{\n  \"schema_version\": \"cross_country_adjudication_v1\",\n  \"artifact\": {\n    \"source_path\": \"paper_v4.Rmd\",\n    \"source_sha256\": \"9c6b03ed3d3703e4a76eb6f35c43201afb08f0479266a1c08b60008e34ff13b4\",\n    \"pdf_path\": \"output/paper_v4.pdf\",\n    \"pdf_sha256\": \"da7b84fd44a1071953c5c2941be53aefb75f2b249476cc2d6e065e5f8463e312\",\n    \"artifact_intact\": true,\n    \"contract_required\": false\n  },\n  \"review_source\": {\n    \"path\": \"reports/refine_ink_review_paper_v4_2026-09-14/feedback-the-foreign-policy-impact-of-trade-based-status-ga-2026-09-14.md\",\n    \"sha256\": \"eb7dc9488e3b6726cee0ddf232250be18f09291797e2a85470b67637af58b88a\"\n  },\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"item\": 2,\n      \"status\": \"PARTIAL\",\n      \"source_locations\": [\n        \"reports/refine_ink_review_paper_v4_2026-09-14/feedback-the-foreign-policy-impact-of-trade-based-status-ga-2026-09-14.md:104-112\",\n        \"paper_v4.Rmd:1882-1923\",\n        \"scripts/diagnostics/analyze_ex_top1_salience.R:46-87\",\n        \"scripts/diagnostics/analyze_ex_top1_salience.R:206-216\",\n        \"scripts/functions.R:2213-2261\",\n        \"scripts/diagnostics/prepare_australia_appendix_bundle_patch.R:75-125\"\n      ],\n      \"defect_evidence\": [\n        \"The manuscript calls this a cross-country audit without disclosing that its underlying matrix has 14 legacy-sample countries rather than the 35 current treated countries.\",\n        \"Only 13 audited countries overlap the current treated sample; Qatar is audit-only and 22 current treated countries were never in this source audit.\",\n        \"The table note does not disclose the display filter or define medium.\",\n        \"Chile and Saudi Arabia retain legacy source-audit entry years that differ from the current treatment target; only Australia was patched.\"\n      ],\n      \"refuting_evidence\": [\n        \"The producer explicitly filters the 14-country matrix to cases without an observed China cue, retaining Australia regardless; the resulting table has nine rows.\",\n        \"Five audited cases are hidden because their China cues were recovered: Chile, Brazil, Uruguay, Saudi Arabia, and Qatar.\",\n        \"Among the 26 current treated countries not displayed, four were audited and hidden by the filter and 22 were not audited; they are not a single group of omitted audit cases.\"\n      ],\n      \"reasoning\": \"The reporting defect exists, but the review overstates the relationship between the 35-country treatment table and the nine-row display. The source audit is a 14-case legacy subset, and the display is a filtered nine-case diagnostic. Accurate disclosure resolves the present reporting problem without inventing searches for the 22 unaudited current cases.\",\n      \"proposed_fix_assessment\": \"safe\",\n      \"implementation_scope\": \"Text, caption, and note only; do not change treatment rules or salience codes.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"item\": 15,\n      \"status\": \"CONFIRMED\",\n      \"source_locations\": [\n        \"reports/refine_ink_review_paper_v4_2026-09-14/feedback-the-foreign-policy-impact-of-trade-based-status-ga-2026-09-14.md:289-306\",\n        \"paper_v4.Rmd:2121-2161\",\n        \"scripts/functions.R:4268-4364\",\n        \"scripts/functions.R:4407-4424\",\n        \"scripts/functions.R:4427-4521\"\n      ],\n      \"defect_evidence\": [\n        \"Table 23 consumes a country-level summary containing only first treatment year, aggregate treated and untreated counts, and panel bounds.\",\n        \"The restricted risk-set producer removes post-entry off-status years and nonqualifying China-top periods, so omitted years cannot be inferred from the displayed aggregates.\",\n        \"The existing store contains 36 qualifying periods among 35 treated countries and 14 short excluded periods across nine of those countries, but Table 23 does not expose them.\",\n        \"Calendar entry-exit bounds cannot safely substitute for observed year lists because some observed periods contain calendar gaps.\"\n      ],\n      \"refuting_evidence\": [],\n      \"reasoning\": \"The review accurately identifies a reproducibility and exposition gap. Existing target objects supply the ingredients, but producing auditable year lists and omission reasons is a new paper-facing transformation and must be implemented as targets from inception.\",\n      \"proposed_fix_assessment\": \"needs_design\",\n      \"implementation_scope\": \"Targets-first audit outputs; no treatment-rule change; retain current table until targets exist and validate.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"replacements\": [\n    {\n      \"item\": 2,\n      \"old\": \"The paragraph at paper_v4.Rmd:1884 that presents an unqualified cross-country audit.\",\n      \"new\": \"To assess the recoverability of public rank language, I use a source audit originally constructed for 14 countries in an earlier no-covariate treated sample. This is not a census of the 35 countries treated in the current goods-only restricted-risk-set specification: 13 audited countries remain in the current treated sample, Qatar does not, and 22 current treated countries were not included in the source audit. The underlying matrix records both recovered and unrecovered China cues. Table 20 is a diagnostic subset: it displays the nine cases in which the China cue is currently coded as unknown; five audited cases with recovered cues are omitted by the display filter. The table distinguishes weak observation from cases in which public rank language about the displaced incumbent is recoverable. Non-recovery is not coded as evidence that a cue was absent because contemporaneous local or official records may be inaccessible or inconsistent with the trade-rank series. Except for Australia, whose displayed year has been reconciled to the current 2009 entry, the table retains the entry windows used in the legacy source audit. Table 21 reports Australia's broad-trade source separately.\",\n      \"implementation_status\": \"ready\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"item\": 2,\n      \"old\": \"Recoverability and metric caveats in the former-incumbent salience audit.\",\n      \"new\": \"Selected unresolved cases from a 14-country legacy source audit of public rank-language recoverability and metric caveats.\",\n      \"implementation_status\": \"ready\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"item\": 2,\n      \"old\": \"The current Table 20 note, which does not disclose the 14-to-9 filter or define medium.\",\n      \"new\": \"The source audit covers 14 countries from an earlier no-covariate treated sample and is not a census of the 35 countries treated in the current goods-only restricted-risk-set specification. Thirteen audited countries remain in the current treated sample; Qatar does not. The table displays the nine cases for which the China cue is coded as unknown; Chile, Brazil, Uruguay, Saudi Arabia, and Qatar have recovered China cues and are omitted from this diagnostic display. For the China cue, `medium` means one countable strong or moderate first-window source with explicit rank language. For the former-incumbent benchmark, `medium` means either one countable source with explicit incumbent-rank or displacement language, or at least two countable trade-coverage records from at least one independent source without a clear top-rank label. Countable sources must be eligible, fall within one year of the source-audit entry year, be coded strong or moderate, enter the benchmark, and not be marked `DO_NOT_COUNT`. `Unknown` means that the incumbent was not identified or that no countable benchmark source was recovered; no case is currently coded `low`. Australia's displayed entry year follows the current annual goods-only panel; other entry years retain the legacy source-audit windows.\",\n      \"implementation_status\": \"ready\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"item\": 15,\n      \"old\": \"Table 23 describes the 35 treated countries in the main goods-only restricted-risk-set specification. For each country, the table reports the first qualifying China-top goods-export year and the number of treated and untreated country-years retained in the estimation panel.\",\n      \"new\": \"Table 23 provides a country-level audit of the 35 treated countries in the main goods-only restricted-risk-set specification. It reports every qualifying entry and exit, the observed years in excluded short China-top periods, the treated years retained by the estimator, and the post-entry off-status years omitted by the restricted risk set. Year ranges are compressed only across consecutive observed calendar years; gaps remain explicit.\",\n      \"implementation_status\": \"deferred_until_targets_exist_and_validate\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"item\": 15,\n      \"old\": \"Treated countries in the main goods-only restricted-risk-set cross-country specification.\",\n      \"new\": \"Country-level audit of retained and omitted years in the main goods-only status-current restricted-risk-set specification.\",\n      \"implementation_status\": \"deferred_until_targets_exist_and_validate\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"item15_target_design\": {\n    \"status\": \"PENDING_IMPLEMENTATION_AND_AUTHORIZED_EXECUTION\",\n    \"no_treatment_rule_change\": true,\n    \"targets\": [\n      \"china_top_m2_goods_status_current_min5_audit_bundle\",\n      \"china_top_m2_goods_status_current_min5_country_year_audit\",\n      \"china_top_m2_goods_status_current_min5_treated_country_table\",\n      \"china_top_m2_goods_status_current_min5_audit_validation\"\n    ],\n    \"inputs\": [\n      \"china_top_m2_goods_panel\",\n      \"china_top_m2_goods_status_current_panel_bundle\",\n      \"china_top_m2_goods_status_current_period_summary\",\n      \"china_top_m2_goods_status_current_unit_summary\"\n    ],\n    \"country_year_fields\": [\n      \"specification\",\n      \"min_duration_years\",\n      \"iso3c\",\n      \"country_name\",\n      \"year\",\n      \"observed_china_top\",\n      \"status_current_period_id\",\n      \"period_entry_year\",\n      \"period_exit_year\",\n      \"period_duration_observed_years\",\n      \"period_calendar_span_years\",\n      \"period_qualifies_min5\",\n      \"retained_in_risk_set\",\n      \"treatment_indicator_retained\",\n      \"row_status\"\n    ],\n    \"row_status_values\": [\n      \"retained_pre_entry_control\",\n      \"retained_qualifying_treated\",\n      \"omitted_missing_required_input\",\n      \"omitted_pre_entry_nonqualifying_china_top\",\n      \"omitted_post_entry_short_china_top_period\",\n      \"omitted_between_qualifying_periods_off_status\",\n      \"omitted_post_final_qualifying_exit_off_status\",\n      \"omitted_other_nonretained\"\n    ],\n    \"display_fields\": [\n      \"Country\",\n      \"ISO3c\",\n      \"Qualifying entries and exits\",\n      \"Excluded short periods\",\n      \"Retained treated years\",\n      \"Omitted off-status years\",\n      \"Treated N\",\n      \"Untreated N\",\n      \"Omitted N\"\n    ],\n    \"required_checks\": [\n      \"unique iso3c-year keys and exhaustive exclusive row_status\",\n      \"retained keys exactly match the risk_set_restricted panel for the 35 treated countries\",\n      \"retained treatment indicator equals one iff the retained row is in a qualifying current China-top period\",\n      \"period boundaries durations and qualification match period_summary\",\n      \"treated and untreated counts match unit_summary by country\",\n      \"display has exactly the 35 current treated ISO3c values\",\n      \"compacted year strings round-trip to actual observed years without filling gaps\",\n      \"omitted_other_nonretained count equals zero\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"checks_performed\": [\n    \"SHA-256 of Rmd, PDF, review, scripts, and target objects\",\n    \"pdftotext -layout inspection of Tables 20 and 23\",\n    \"read-only deserialization of existing RDS and target objects\",\n    \"35 treated versus 14 audited versus 9 displayed set comparison\",\n    \"inspection of producer filter and medium coding rules\",\n    \"inspection of status-current restricted-risk-set row filter\",\n    \"inspection of period and unit summaries\"\n  ],\n  \"limitations\": [\n    \"No targets rebuild or freshness validation was run.\",\n    \"No new source searches were performed; 22 current treated countries remain outside the source audit.\",\n    \"Item 2 text does not synchronize legacy Chile or Saudi Arabia search windows or remove Qatar from the historical audit.\",\n    \"Item 15 requires authorized edits to scripts/functions.R, _targets.R, and paper_v4.Rmd, followed by target execution and validation.\"\n  ],\n  \"summary\": {\n    \"total\": 2,\n    \"confirmed\": 1,\n    \"partial\": 1,\n    \"refuted\": 0,\n    \"unresolved\": 0,\n    \"verdict\": \"READY_FOR_IMPLEMENTATION\"\n  }\n}\n\n--- sdid prereq ---\n{\n  \"schema_version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"adjudication_id\": \"paper-v4-sdid:da7b84fd44a1:refine-20260914\",\n  \"source\": {\n    \"reviewed_artifact\": \"output/paper_v4.pdf\",\n    \"sha256\": \"da7b84fd44a1071953c5c2941be53aefb75f2b249476cc2d6e065e5f8463e312\",\n    \"artifact_intact\": true,\n    \"source_rmd\": \"paper_v4.Rmd\",\n    \"source_rmd_sha256\": \"9c6b03ed3d3703e4a76eb6f35c43201afb08f0479266a1c08b60008e34ff13b4\",\n    \"baseline_manifest\": \"reports/refine_ink_review_paper_v4_2026-09-14/execution/baseline_manifest.json\",\n    \"identity_note\": \"The active Rmd and PDF are byte-identical to the frozen baseline copies, and the five quoted passages occur in both source and rendered PDF.\"\n  },\n  \"contract\": {\n    \"required\": false,\n    \"path\": null,\n    \"sha256\": null,\n    \"contract_id\": null,\n    \"artifact_sha256\": null,\n    \"status\": null,\n    \"stale\": false\n  },\n  \"review_sources\": [\n    {\n      \"review_id\": \"REFINE\",\n      \"path\": \"reports/refine_ink_review_paper_v4_2026-09-14/feedback-the-foreign-policy-impact-of-trade-based-status-ga-2026-09-14.md\",\n      \"sha256\": \"eb7dc9488e3b6726cee0ddf232250be18f09291797e2a85470b67637af58b88a\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"review_id\": \"SELECTION\",\n      \"path\": \"reports/refine_ink_review_paper_v4_2026-09-14/items_to_address.md\",\n      \"sha256\": \"d0220df748585215fc3ce14786e555546134d1e25534470ee153b1872437ea25\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"finding_id\": \"REFINE-006\",\n      \"item\": 6,\n      \"source_review\": \"REFINE\",\n      \"quoted_finding\": \"Table 5 does not fully define the exposure variables, baseline periods, the meaning of x 2008-2009, or the treatment of lower-order terms.\",\n      \"type\": \"exposition\",\n      \"severity\": \"unspecified\",\n      \"scientific_dimension\": \"fidelity of implementation\",\n      \"held_decision\": false,\n      \"status\": \"CONFIRMED\",\n      \"source_locations\": [\n        \"paper_v4.Rmd:754\",\n        \"paper_v4.Rmd:805\",\n        \"paper_v4.Rmd:867\",\n        \"output/paper_v4.pdf:p.23, Table 5 and preceding paragraph\"\n      ],\n      \"defect_evidence\": [\n        \"The Table 5 labels say only Primary share, Agriculture/mining, Price exposure, and Prior China share x 2008-2009; the note says only that the measures use external goods exports and that the interaction includes the first treated year.\",\n        \"The active producer defines country means over 2004-2008 for primary goods, agriculture, mining and energy, and China's goods-export share; the manuscript does not report those definitions.\",\n        \"The active producer includes only standardized time-varying interactions in the four diagnostic fits. Fixed exposure levels are omitted because they are absorbed by unit effects, and the common 2008-2009 indicator is absorbed by time effects; this lower-order-term logic is absent from the paper.\",\n        \"The price row is a distinct construction: 2004-2008 export-composition weights multiply World Bank Pink Sheet log-price changes relative to 2007 before the 2008-2009 activation and standardization.\"\n      ],\n      \"refuting_evidence\": [],\n      \"mechanical_checks\": [\n        \"Inspected scripts/diagnostics/audit_brazil_sdid_commodity_no_covariates.R:97-151 and the upstream construction at scripts/diagnostics/audit_brazil_sdid_predetermined_commodity_controls.R:190-257,293-326.\",\n        \"Matched all six rows and values to data/processed/diagnostics/brazil_sdid_commodity_no_covariates/table_5_sdid_specification_results.csv; smoke_test is FALSE.\",\n        \"Confirmed the producer uses no lower-order exposure levels in specifications at lines 121-127.\"\n      ],\n      \"reasoning\": \"The diagnostics are implemented coherently, but the rendered table cannot be interpreted from the manuscript alone. This is a bounded reporting defect; it does not require re-estimation.\",\n      \"proposed_fix_assessment\": \"safe\",\n      \"disposition\": \"Add the exact 2004-2008 exposure definitions, the 2008-2009 activation rule, the price-index construction, standardization, and the absorbed lower-order-term explanation to the paragraph/note. Keep the main covariate-free specification and all estimates unchanged.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"finding_id\": \"REFINE-018\",\n      \"item\": 18,\n      \"source_review\": \"REFINE\",\n      \"quoted_finding\": \"The uncertainty discussion conflates the placebo-based standard error, the exhaustive placebo-in-space rank, and the normal approximation used for p-values and confidence intervals.\",\n      \"type\": \"method\",\n      \"severity\": \"unspecified\",\n      \"scientific_dimension\": \"inference\",\n      \"held_decision\": false,\n      \"status\": \"CONFIRMED\",\n      \"source_locations\": [\n        \"paper_v4.Rmd:308-310\",\n        \"paper_v4.Rmd:338\",\n        \"paper_v4.Rmd:654-661\",\n        \"output/paper_v4.pdf:p.11\"\n      ],\n      \"defect_evidence\": [\n        \"Line 308 incorrectly calls the standard error a normal-approximation quantity and describes the directional rank as the procedure used to compute uncertainty.\",\n        \"The reported SE is instead a synthdid placebo SE: se_sdid takes the finite-population standard deviation of 20,000 seeded placebo resamples for the preferred fit.\",\n        \"The conventional two-sided p-value and 95 percent interval are then calculated from the estimate and placebo SE with a normal approximation.\",\n        \"The rank is a separate, deterministic placebo-in-space exercise: every one of 96 units is treated once, yielding directional rank 3/96 and absolute bilateral rank 7/96.\"\n      ],\n      \"refuting_evidence\": [],\n      \"mechanical_checks\": [\n        \"Inspected scripts/functions.R:1072-1151 and scripts/diagnostics/sdid_placebo_helpers.R:230-297 for the 20,000-resample placebo SE algorithm.\",\n        \"Inspected scripts/diagnostics/sdid_placebo_helpers.R:299-380 and rank_inference.csv for the exhaustive, no-RNG rank procedure.\",\n        \"Confirmed main_summary.csv records estimate -0.2727714076, placebo SE 0.1306079433, normal p 0.0367550198, directional rank 3/96, bilateral rank 7/96, seed 20260520, and 20,000 SE replications.\"\n      ],\n      \"reasoning\": \"The numerical outputs and result-table labels already distinguish the quantities, but the design paragraph assigns the wrong source to the standard error and merges three logically separate inferential summaries.\",\n      \"proposed_fix_assessment\": \"safe\",\n      \"disposition\": \"Replace the uncertainty paragraph with an explicit three-step account. Do not change estimates, SEs, ranks, or the held convention that the directional rank is theory-aligned and the absolute rank is a conservative sensitivity assessment.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"finding_id\": \"REFINE-020\",\n      \"item\": 20,\n      \"source_review\": \"REFINE\",\n      \"quoted_finding\": \"The displayed SCM and SDiD objectives omit definitions of the positive weights on treated units and post-treatment periods, so a literal reading makes the treatment term disappear.\",\n      \"type\": \"method\",\n      \"severity\": \"unspecified\",\n      \"scientific_dimension\": \"fidelity of implementation\",\n      \"held_decision\": false,\n      \"status\": \"CONFIRMED\",\n      \"source_locations\": [\n        \"paper_v4.Rmd:1426-1448\",\n        \"output/paper_v4.pdf:pp.46-47\"\n      ],\n      \"defect_evidence\": [\n        \"The text defines only donor-unit weights and reports only pre-treatment time weights, but the objective sums over every unit-period cell without defining full-sample weights.\",\n        \"Without fixed positive weights on treated units and post-treatment periods, the displayed notation does not show how treated-post cells enter and identify the ATT.\"\n      ],\n      \"refuting_evidence\": [],\n      \"mechanical_checks\": [\n        \"Inspected the installed synthdid 0.0.9 implementation of synthdid_estimate: the estimator uses c(-omega, rep(1/N1,N1)) and c(-lambda, rep(1/T1,T1)).\",\n        \"Confirmed the active preferred target is a synthdid_estimate with N0=95, T0=12 and no covariate array; no implementation failure was found.\"\n      ],\n      \"reasoning\": \"The defect is in exposition only. The software gives donor controls optimized weights, treated units uniform weight 1/N1, pre-treatment periods optimized weights, and post-treatment periods uniform weight 1/T1. The current equation becomes complete once those full vectors are defined.\",\n      \"proposed_fix_assessment\": \"safe\",\n      \"disposition\": \"Define N0, N1, T0, and T1 and the full unit/time weight vectors immediately before the objectives. State that treated and post-treatment cells receive positive uniform weights.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"finding_id\": \"REFINE-031\",\n      \"item\": 31,\n      \"source_review\": \"REFINE\",\n      \"quoted_finding\": \"The covariate comparison may contain a time-invariant geographic-distance term absorbed by unit effects and a power-gap term collinear with country power and time effects.\",\n      \"type\": \"scope_or_consistency\",\n      \"severity\": \"unspecified\",\n      \"scientific_dimension\": \"fidelity of implementation\",\n      \"held_decision\": false,\n      \"status\": \"PARTIAL\",\n      \"source_locations\": [\n        \"paper_v4.Rmd:225-227\",\n        \"paper_v4.Rmd:306\",\n        \"paper_v4.Rmd:548-661, Table 3\",\n        \"output/paper_v4.pdf:pp.11,18\",\n        \"scripts/functions.R:180-210\",\n        \"scripts/functions.R:681-721\"\n      ],\n      \"defect_evidence\": [\n        \"Geographic distance to the United States is time-invariant, remains in the 13-variable synthdid covariate array, and its stored coefficient is 7.96e-19. It supplies no separate adjustment under the unit-effect parametrization even though Table 3 marks it as included.\",\n        \"The manuscript does not say whether this variable was absorbed, dropped, or transformed.\"\n      ],\n      \"refuting_evidence\": [\n        \"The actual power variable is us_power_gap = abs(us_power - gpi), not the signed difference assumed by the reviewer.\",\n        \"The absolute value breaks the alleged exact linear identity with country GPI and annual U.S. power/time effects. The stored current-covariate fit gives us_power_gap coefficient -0.008069, rather than zero.\",\n        \"The preferred fit has a 96 x 19 x 0 covariate array; this issue cannot alter the main covariate-free ATT.\"\n      ],\n      \"mechanical_checks\": [\n        \"Read get_gpi_data at scripts/functions.R:180-210 and cov_matrix/simple_fit at scripts/functions.R:681-755.\",\n        \"Read the stored targets synth_fit and synth_fit_no_time_varying_covariates without rebuilding them; the former has 13 beta coefficients and the latter has zero covariates.\",\n        \"Verified distance_us beta 7.959e-19 and us_power_gap beta -8.069e-03 in the stored comparison fit.\"\n      ],\n      \"reasoning\": \"The distance part is correct and underreported. The signed-power-gap collinearity claim does not match the implemented absolute differential and is refuted. The paper should clarify both facts without implying that the covariate comparison validates the main estimate.\",\n      \"proposed_fix_assessment\": \"safe\",\n      \"disposition\": \"Clarify that distance remains in the comparison array but is absorbed/inert, define the power gap as the absolute annual GPI difference, and reiterate that the covariate-adjusted model is only a comparison. Leave the preferred no-covariate fit unchanged.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"finding_id\": \"REFINE-032\",\n      \"item\": 32,\n      \"source_review\": \"REFINE\",\n      \"quoted_finding\": \"The paper reverses the role of SDiD time weights and implies that unit and time weights are constructed from the same pre-treatment information.\",\n      \"type\": \"method\",\n      \"severity\": \"unspecified\",\n      \"scientific_dimension\": \"fidelity of implementation\",\n      \"held_decision\": false,\n      \"status\": \"CONFIRMED\",\n      \"source_locations\": [\n        \"paper_v4.Rmd:223\",\n        \"paper_v4.Rmd:302\",\n        \"paper_v4.Rmd:1424\",\n        \"output/paper_v4.pdf:pp.8,11,46\"\n      ],\n      \"defect_evidence\": [\n        \"Line 1424 says time periods are weighted for comparability to the pre-treatment period; the implemented lambda optimization has the opposite target.\",\n        \"Lines 223 and 302 imply that both unit and time weights are constructed from pre-treatment information or from generic pre/post comparability.\",\n        \"In synthdid 0.0.9, optimized lambda lies on pre-treatment periods and targets the vector of control units' average post-treatment outcomes.\"\n      ],\n      \"refuting_evidence\": [],\n      \"mechanical_checks\": [\n        \"Inspected synthdid_estimate, collapsed.form, sc.weight.fw, and sc.weight.fw.covariates in the installed synthdid 0.0.9 namespace.\",\n        \"Confirmed collapsed.form replaces the post-treatment block by each control unit's post-period mean before lambda optimization.\",\n        \"Confirmed Table 10 correctly reports only the optimized pre-treatment lambda vector; the defect is the verbal description, not the stored weights.\"\n      ],\n      \"reasoning\": \"Unit weights use pre-treatment outcome histories to approximate the treated unit. Time weights use control outcomes from both sides of onset: weighted pre-treatment control outcomes approximate the controls' average post-treatment outcomes. The manuscript currently merges these operations.\",\n      \"proposed_fix_assessment\": \"safe\",\n      \"disposition\": \"Correct the three local descriptions and use uniform-weight language for classic DiD. Coordinate the definitions with item 20 so the appendix does not repeat or contradict itself.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"replacements\": [\n    {\n      \"item\": 6,\n      \"location\": \"paper_v4.Rmd:867-879, Table 5 note\",\n      \"old\": \"Primary-goods measures use external goods exports only. \\\",\\n  \\\"The 2008-2009 interactions include the first treated year and are mechanism robustness checks, not preferred total-effect specifications.\",\n      \"new\": \"The exposure baselines are country means over 2004--2008: primary goods as a share of external goods exports, its Agriculture and Mining and Energy components, and China as a share of external goods exports. `x 2008--2009` means that the fixed 2004--2008 exposure is multiplied by an indicator for 2008 and 2009 and then standardized over the estimation panel. \\\",\\n  \\\"The price diagnostic instead weights World Bank Pink Sheet log-price changes relative to 2007 by the country's 2004--2008 Agriculture, Energy, and Metals and Minerals export shares, activates that index in 2008--2009, and standardizes it. \\\",\\n  \\\"Only these time-varying interactions enter the four diagnostic specifications: exposure levels are time-invariant and absorbed by unit effects, while the common 2008--2009 indicator is absorbed by time effects. \\\",\\n  \\\"Because 2009 is the first treated year, these are mechanism robustness checks rather than preferred total-effect specifications.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"item\": 18,\n      \"location\": \"paper_v4.Rmd:308-310\",\n      \"old\": \"To compute the uncertainty of estimates, I use a one-sided placebo-in-space rank of the Brazil estimate within the distribution of placebo estimates obtained by reassigning treatment to each unit from the donor pool. For robustness, I also report the standard error calculated from the normal approximation native to the SDiD estimator. I use a one-sided hypothesis test, since the theory is directional (a treated unit should move its ideal point toward China), and report the two-sided test as a conservative sensitivity assessment.\",\n      \"new\": \"I report three distinct inferential summaries for the preferred Brazil estimate. First, the placebo-based standard error is the finite-population standard deviation of 20,000 seeded synthdid placebo resamples. Second, I combine that placebo standard error with a two-sided normal approximation to report the conventional p-value and 95 percent confidence interval. Third, I report deterministic placebo-in-space ranks obtained by reassigning treatment once to Brazil and to every donor: the directional rank counts estimates at least as negative as Brazil's, while the bilateral rank compares absolute magnitudes. The directional rank follows the theory's prediction of convergence; the bilateral rank is a conservative sensitivity assessment.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"item\": 20,\n      \"location\": \"paper_v4.Rmd:1437, before the SDiD objective\",\n      \"old\": \"SDiD combines unit weights (like SCM) with unit fixed effects (like DiD) and time weights (unique to SDiD), addressing the limitations of both. The basic SDiD estimating equation is:\",\n      \"new\": \"SDiD combines unit weights (like SCM) with unit fixed effects (like DiD) and time weights. Let $N_0$ and $N_1$ denote the numbers of control and treated units and $T_0$ and $T_1$ the numbers of pre- and post-treatment periods. In the full unit-weight vector, controls receive the optimized nonnegative donor weights, which sum to one, and each treated unit receives the fixed positive weight $1/N_1$. In the full time-weight vector, pre-treatment periods receive optimized nonnegative weights, which sum to one, and each post-treatment period receives the fixed positive weight $1/T_1$. Thus treated-post cells enter the objective with positive weight. The basic SDiD estimating equation is:\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"item\": 20,\n      \"location\": \"paper_v4.Rmd:1437, SCM definition\",\n      \"old\": \"Here $\\\\hat{w}^{\\\\text{SCM}}_i$ is the donor-unit weight assigned to unit $i$.\",\n      \"new\": \"Here $\\\\hat{w}^{\\\\text{SCM}}_i$ denotes the full unit-weight vector: an optimized nonnegative weight for each control unit and the fixed positive weight $1/N_1$ for each treated unit.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"item\": 31,\n      \"location\": \"paper_v4.Rmd:306\",\n      \"old\": \"The preferred specification uses no covariates because time-varying post-2009 values may induce post-treatment bias. A model specification with time-varying variables uses trade, power, ideology, macroeconomic stress, and institutional variables to control for potential confounding. The similarity of the estimates indicates low sensitivity to post-treatment adjustment, suggesting the results are not driven by the covariates. Commodity composition and price interactions are also treated as robustness or mechanism diagnostics, especially because the 2008--2009 interaction includes the first treated year.\",\n      \"new\": \"The preferred specification uses no covariates because time-varying post-2009 values may induce post-treatment bias. The current-covariate comparison passes the country-year variables listed in Table 3 to synthdid. Geographic distance to the United States is time-invariant: it remains in that comparison array but is absorbed by the unit-effect parametrization and supplies no separate adjustment. The power gap is the absolute annual difference between the U.S. and country Global Power Index values, rather than a signed difference, so it is not mechanically collinear with country power and time effects. This covariate-adjusted model is retained only as a sensitivity comparison; the preferred specification remains covariate-free. Commodity composition and price interactions are separate robustness or mechanism diagnostics, especially because the 2008--2009 interaction includes the first treated year.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"item\": 32,\n      \"location\": \"paper_v4.Rmd:223\",\n      \"old\": \"SDiD estimates Brazil's average post-2009 gap relative to a weighted synthetic counterfactual, using pre-treatment information to construct unit and time weights [@arkhangelsky_etal2021].\",\n      \"new\": \"SDiD estimates Brazil's average post-2009 gap relative to a weighted synthetic counterfactual. Unit weights are learned from pre-treatment outcome histories, whereas the optimized pre-treatment time weights use control outcomes before onset and the controls' average outcome after onset [@arkhangelsky_etal2021].\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"item\": 32,\n      \"location\": \"paper_v4.Rmd:302\",\n      \"old\": \"And, unique to the method, it weights the time periods, choosing the ones most comparable pre- and post-treatment.\",\n      \"new\": \"It also weights pre-treatment periods so that the controls' weighted pre-treatment outcomes approximate their average post-treatment outcomes.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"item\": 32,\n      \"location\": \"paper_v4.Rmd:1424\",\n      \"old\": \"While SDiD assigns larger weights to control units more similar to the treated unit and to time periods more comparable to the pre-treatment period, classic DiD does not use any weights at all.\",\n      \"new\": \"SDiD assigns larger unit weights to control units whose pre-treatment outcome paths help reproduce the treated unit. Separately, it assigns optimized weights to pre-treatment periods so that their weighted control-unit outcomes approximate the controls' average post-treatment outcomes. Unit weights therefore use pre-treatment outcome histories, whereas time weights use control outcomes from both sides of treatment onset. Classic DiD corresponds to uniform weighting in this comparison.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"item29_caption_prerequisites\": {\n    \"purpose\": \"Methodological prerequisites for the later Figure 2 caption correction; item 29 is not adjudicated in this record.\",\n    \"current_figure\": \"The PNG is generated from the stored no-covariate synthdid fit by plot.synthdid_estimate. It plots the unshifted Brazil and weighted-donor trajectories and overlays synthdid's difference-in-differences diagram; the arrow denotes the estimator.\",\n    \"estimand_identity\": \"With one treated unit and no covariates, ATT = [Brazil post mean - donor-weighted post mean] - [lambda-weighted Brazil pre outcome - donor-and-lambda-weighted pre outcome]. The raw vertical separation of the two plotted trajectories in any post year, or even their post-period average separation, is not generally the ATT because the lambda-weighted pre level gap must be netted out.\",\n    \"caption_requirements\": [\n      \"Call the two lines observed Brazil and the unshifted weighted donor trajectory.\",\n      \"Describe the arrow as the level-adjusted SDiD ATT, equal to the average post-treatment contrast net of the SDiD lambda-weighted pre-treatment contrast.\",\n      \"Do not call the raw post-treatment vertical distance between the paths the ATT.\",\n      \"Keep the no-covariate specification, 1997-2015 window, 20,000-replication placebo SE, and existing ATT unchanged.\"\n    ],\n    \"verification_after_edit\": [\n      \"Confirm the figure still comes from synth_fit_no_time_varying_covariates and that the plotted arrow is supplied by synthdid_plot rather than a raw-gap annotation.\",\n      \"Render and inspect the Figure 2 page, checking that caption wording clearly distinguishes the raw trajectories from the adjusted arrow.\",\n      \"Compare the displayed ATT and SE against main_summary.csv; no model rerun is needed for a caption-only change.\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"implementation_checks\": [\n    \"Apply only the replacement text; do not change numerical values, estimands, covariate sets, targets, or output producers.\",\n    \"Run a source search to ensure the superseded descriptions of the SE and time weights no longer remain elsewhere in the manuscript.\",\n    \"Render the manuscript and inspect the pages containing the identification paragraph, Table 5, and the SDiD appendix equations.\",\n    \"Confirm inline values remain -0.273, 0.131, [-0.529, -0.017], 3/96, and 7/96 and Table 5 values remain byte-for-byte numerically unchanged.\",\n    \"If any new estimate, diagnostic, or paper-facing data transformation becomes necessary, specify it as a target/file target first. The current Table 5 producer remains listed as P1 outside the graph in TARGETS_MIGRATION.md.\"\n  ],\n  \"unresolved_limits\": [\n    \"No model, placebo, bootstrap, target, or manuscript render was executed in this adjudication.\",\n    \"The local synthdid 0.0.9 implementation and stored target objects were inspected; this record does not assess behavior under a future package version.\",\n    \"Table 5's paper-facing CSV still comes from a producer outside the current targets graph. The proposed prose correction relies only on existing frozen outputs and does not cure that separate migration debt.\"\n  ],\n  \"summary\": {\n    \"total\": 5,\n    \"confirmed\": 4,\n    \"partial\": 1,\n    \"refuted\": 0,\n    \"unresolved\": 0,\n    \"held_decisions\": 0\n  },\n  \"adjudication\": {\n    \"verdict\": \"READY_FOR_IMPLEMENTATION\",\n    \"checked_at\": \"2026-09-14T13:28:25-03:00\",\n    \"reasons\": [\n      \"All five items are resolved against the exact frozen artifact and active implementation.\",\n      \"The fixes are bounded manuscript-exposition changes and require no re-estimation.\",\n      \"The preferred covariate-free SDiD specification and all reported numerical results remain unchanged.\"\n    ]\n  }\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
