erability            Local statistics conflict with\n--\n2536-ment: 80.0 percent for “china-brazil relations” and 83.3 percent for “diplomacy.”\n2537-\n2538-\n2539-\n2540-\n2541-                                                    62\n2542-\f8.9     Cross-Country: Goods-Only Treated Countries\n2543-\n2544-Table 23 describes the 35 treated countries in the main goods-only restricted-risk-set speci-\n2545-fication. For each country, the table reports the first qualifying China-top goods-export year\n2546-and the number of treated and untreated country-years retained in the estimation panel.\n2547-\n2548:Table 23: Treated countries in the main goods-only restricted-risk-set cross-country spec-\n2549-ification.\n2550-\n2551: Country               ISO3c   Treatment year   Treated years    Pre/other untreated years   First panel year   Last panel year\n2552-\n2553: Sudan                 SDN         2000                6                    10                    1990               2005\n2554: Solomon Islands       SLB         2003               20                    13                    1990               2022\n2555- South Korea           KOR         2003               20                    12                    1991               2022\n2556- Cuba                  CUB         2004               18                    14                    1990               2022\n2557- Oman                  OMN         2004               19                    13                    1990               2022\n2558- Philippines           PHL         2005               18                    15                    1990               2022\n2559- Yemen                 YEM         2005               11                    13                    1991               2015\n2560- Mauritania            MRT         2006               17                    15                    1990               2022\n2561- Angola                AGO         2007               16                    17                    1990    